      "role": "user",
      "content": "Right, so they used these \"scientific\" or \"sociological\" justifications to make it sound objective. Can you expand on that \"social friction\" part? Specifically, how did they argue that racial integration would lead to a \"breakdown of social fabric\" or \"public peace\"? I want to see if they used specific tropes about certain groups being unable to coexist with others, or if they argued that one group's presence would naturally degrade another's culture or standard of living. I need to capture the actual reasoning they used to make those claims seem like rational policy decisions.",
